In the Horvitz--Thompson sampling-total specialization of \citet{AronowSamii2013}, with singleton observation probabilities \(\pi_{\{i\}}>0\) and assignment score coordinates
\[
v_{z,i}=\frac{\mathbb 1\{i\in O_z\}}{\pi_{\{i\}}},
\]
the simplified \(a_{ik}=b_{ik}=2\) Aronow--Samii observed-data correction table is
\[
g_z^{\mathrm{AS}}(\theta|_{O_z})
:=
\sum_{\substack{i,k\in I\\ \pi_{\{i,k\}}>0}}
\mathbb 1\{\{i,k\}\subseteq O_z\}
\frac{(\pi_{\{i,k\}}-\pi_{\{i\}}\pi_{\{k\}})\theta_i\theta_k}
{\pi_{\{i,k\}}\pi_{\{i\}}\pi_{\{k\}}}
+
\sum_{\substack{i\ne k\\ \pi_{\{i,k\}}=0}}
\left\{
\frac{\mathbb 1\{i\in O_z\}\theta_i}{2\pi_{\{i\}}}
+
\frac{\mathbb 1\{k\in O_z\}\theta_k}{2\pi_{\{k\}}}
\right\}.
\]
The expected Aronow--Samii correction is
\[
b_{\mathrm{AS}}(\theta)
:=
\sum_{z\in Z}p_z g_z^{\mathrm{AS}}(\theta|_{O_z}).
\]
